      "node_id": "kg_doc_8",
      "node_type": "kg",
      "content": "The 2016–17 Vermont Catamounts men's basketball team represented the University of Vermont during the 2016–17 NCAA Division I men's basketball season. The Catamounts, led by sixth-year head coach John Becker, played their home games at Patrick Gym in Burlington, Vermont and were members of the America East Conference. They finished the season 29–6, 16–0 in America East play to win the America East regular season championship. In the America East Tournament, they defeated Maine, New Hampshire and Albany to win the tournament championship. As a result, they received the conference's automatic bid to the NCAA Tournament. As a No. 13 seed in the Midwest region, they lost to No. 4-seeded Purdue in the first round.",
      "depth": 0,
